## Project Description
This project develops a C program for calculating electricity bills for a rural electricity co-operative. It considers meter readings, electricity consumption, tariff slabs, fixed charges, meter rollover, and accurate monetary calculations.

## Objectives
1. Understand the electricity billing problem.
2. Select suitable C data types.
3. Use constants and macros.
4. Organize code using header files.
5. Read and display customer information.
6. Perform safe type conversions.
7. Understand the C compilation process.
8. Implement an electricity billing program.
9. Test normal and exceptional cases.
10. Design a scalable smart-meter billing solution.

## Folder Description
Each task has a separate folder containing its explanation and relevant C source code. The Screenshots folder is reserved for genuine screenshots captured during program execution.

## Compilation
Compile a C file using GCC:

```bash
gcc filename.c -o program
```

Run on Linux:

```bash
./program
```

On Windows:

```bash
program.exe
```

## Note
The tariff values in the demonstration program are illustrative. Replace them with the official tariff values provided by the faculty, if different.
